{#- T3 — code review. One repo, scoped to the whole tree, a directory, an
    explicit file list, or a diff. Context: docs/prompt-context.md. -#}
{% set repo = repos[0] -%}
You are reviewing a change to **{{ repo.name }}**. Give the review you would give a
teammate: direct, specific, and focused on what matters.

Generated {{ generated_at }}.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONTEXT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Repository: {{ repo.name }} · {{ repo.category }}
{% if repo.git and repo.git.branch -%}
Branch: {{ repo.git.branch }}
{% endif -%}
Primary languages:
{% for l in repo.languages[:5] -%}
  - {{ l.language }} ({{ l.percentage | round(1) }}%)
{% endfor -%}
{% if repo.technologies %}
Stack: {% for t in repo.technologies %}{{ t.tech }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% endif -%}
{% if repo.findings %}
Outstanding security findings (context for the review, not necessarily part of
this change):
{% for f in repo.findings[:10] -%}
  - {{ f.advisory_id }} — {{ f.package }}@{{ f.version }} ({{ f.severity }})
{% endfor -%}
{% endif %}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT YOU ARE REVIEWING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
{% if scope.kind == "diff" -%}
A diff. Review the change itself — do not review unchanged surrounding code except
where the change breaks an assumption it relied on.

{{ scope.description }}
{% elif scope.kind == "directory" -%}
Everything under `{{ scope.path }}`.
{% elif scope.kind == "files" -%}
A specific set of files ({{ files | length }}).
{% else -%}
The whole repository as it currently stands.
{% endif %}
{% if files -%}
{% for file in files %}
### {{ file.path }}{% if file.language %} ({{ file.language }}){% endif %}

```{{ file.language | lower if file.language else "" }}
{{ file.content }}
```
{% endfor -%}
{% endif %}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HOW TO REPORT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Group findings by severity: **Blocking**, **Should fix**, **Nit**. For each
finding give `path:line`, what is wrong, and the concrete fix. Cover, in order:

1. Correctness — logic errors, edge cases, race conditions, error handling.
2. Security — injection, auth, unsafe deserialization, secrets, unvalidated input.
3. Interface and contract — breaking changes, unclear names, missing docs on
   public surface.
4. Tests — untested new behavior, tests that would not catch the bug they imply.
5. Clarity — only where it genuinely impedes a reader.

If a whole category has nothing worth saying, write one line saying so. End with a
one-sentence overall assessment: is this ready to merge, close, or does it need
another pass?
